<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="30989d09">&lt;p&gt;
    The PM tracks and monitors the project work packages, milestones, work products and the associated resources,
    timeframes and dependencies. The PM proactively manages progress across the project (end-to-end), including assessing
    the team’s ability to meet key milestones and the target dates.&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;br /&gt;
    Using knowledge of the actual resources available for the project and additional planning information, the project plan
    is transformed into an actionable plan:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Stages and activities expand in detail (e.g., into tasks, work steps);
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The tentative timeline becomes a schedule of events;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Specific individuals fill project roles such as team leader and team member;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Updates to the risk and quality management approaches occur;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Cost management is established; and
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The operational organization and governance structure of the project forms.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    As all of these elements come together, they are documented in enablers such as the Project Charter and other enablers
    that support this phase.&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;br /&gt;
    Planning adjustments occur during this phase for a variety of reasons. The PM works with the client to manage
    adjustments and maintain balance between the scope, timeline, and financials of the project. It is possible that a
    scope and fee change occurs during this phase, however, work (and cost) increases in one work stream or activity are
    often offset by decreases in another, and only after re-establishing the baseline are any net scope changes addressed.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Along with the planning activities, the project governance structure and communications protocols should be
        established.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Project governance addresses roles and responsibilities.&lt;br /&gt;
        The communications protocols address how these parties should interchange information.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
